Leaner generated VU1 blocks (tools/vu1/vu1n_gen.py, ps2_vu1_native.h), bit-identical results:
- operand normalisation (Inf/NaN -> +-FLT_MAX) as an unsigned minimum of the magnitude with FLT_MAX plus the sign:
  4 operations instead of 6 (blendv);
- no clamp after ADD / SUB / MUL of VF operands: blocks run with round-toward-zero and FTZ/DAZ, where finite operands
  saturate at FLT_MAX; maddc clamps only its rare wide path (macVal counts FLT_MAX as overflow like an infinity, so
  the MAC flags are unchanged);
- VF operands read once per block into locals (normalised once) and ACC kept in a local until written; every write
  still goes to the VU1 state.
Measured on 4000 recorded combat programs (replay, 4 alternating rounds): 157.3 -> 143.8 ms (-8.6%), 0 differ.
Save route, full screen, 4 alternating pairs: 51.0 -> 56.9 FPS mean, combat 50.9 -> 55.1 FPS, 4 of 4 pairs.

